<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32294" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oeā^grus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οἴαγρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of</i>
			
			<i>Thrace</i>, <i>the father of
			Orpheus</i>, Ov Ib. 484; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 14</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oeā^grĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οἰάγριος</span>, <i>Œagrian</i>,
				<b>poet.</b> for <i>Thracian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oeagrius Hebrus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 524</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Haemus,</span>”
				<i>where Orpheus was torn in pieces</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 219</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dulcius Oeagrios pulsabat pectine nervos,</span>”
				<i>played on the cithara like Orpheus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					4, 463</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
